Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 17:52:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 36/36] Stop sending routed_experts; finish the handoff docs

enable_return_routed_experts = false on both engines. With enable_router_replay
= false the trainer already discarded routed_experts on arrival (train.py:571),
so 95.5% of every byte crossing a 7.5%-loss link was going straight to the bin.
Measured on both engines: the same 64-token response fell from 71064 to about
10500 bytes, 6.8x less on the wire.

The two flags must move together. Reverting one alone either stops the trainer
or wastes the bandwidth again.

Docs finished for the handoff: HANDOFF.md rewritten around the network
topology, which explains most of the behaviour, and carrying the open router
replay question, today's mistakes, and the ranked next steps. AGENTS.md now
describes x25 and states the arithmetic plainly -- at 13 rollouts a minute a
batch of 1024 is a 79 minute step. CHANGES.md covers the payload change,
tune_wan.sh, the checkpoint fix and the sweep harness. PERFORMANCE.md holds the
measurements.

